    "Answer": "2 × 10⁻⁷ N", "Image": "",
    "Explaination": "The force per unit length between two parallel conductors is F/l = μ0·I1·I2/(2πd). With I1 = I2 = 1 A, d = 1 m and μ0 = 4π×10⁻⁷: F/l = (4π×10⁻⁷ × 1 × 1)/(2π × 1) = 2×10⁻⁷ N/m. This is the basis of the definition of the ampere. Hence the force is 2 × 10⁻⁷ N."
