  {
    "Question": "The unit of flux is the same as that of",
    "A": "Reluctance", "B": "Resistance", "C": "Permeance", "D": "Pole strength",
    "Answer": "Pole strength", "Image": "",
    "Explaination": "Magnetic flux φ is measured in weber (Wb). Pole strength m is defined such that flux φ = m, so pole strength also has the unit weber (A·m in some conventions but dimensionally the same as flux). Reluctance is AT/Wb, resistance is ohm, and permeance is Wb/AT. Hence flux has the same unit as pole strength."
